WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.710
JEWEL LANGEVINE: Hello, my
name is Jewel Langevine,

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:11.670
and today I am going to take you
through my journey of becoming

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:13.740
Google Cloud Certified.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.620
I'll give you an
introduction to who I am,

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.330
a bit about my
certification journey,

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.120
the impact it has
had on my career,

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.230
and then leave you
with some takeaways.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.680
So let's get started
with an introduction.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.670
My name is Jewel, and I
am a solution engineer

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.440
at Google Cloud.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.950
I am currently a Google Cloud
Certified professional data

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.590
engineer, associate
cloud engineer,

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:42.870
and professional
cloud architect.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:45.060
I'm really, really
happy to be here today

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:48.990
to share my story with you.

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:51.230
It's interesting to think
of my journey as a three

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:53.390
by three by three.

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:57.770
Three countries, three states,
and three certifications.

00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:00.560
I was born in Guyana
in South America.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.500
I grew up in the
Bahamas, and in the USA,

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.170
I have lived in Texas
and New York City

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:10.840
before eventually moving to
California for my current role.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:14.510
I have always been an
inquisitive person since birth.

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:17.150
For example, in
Guyana, my father

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:20.820
used to buy mint candies
before church every week

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:23.420
and I used to divvy them
up amongst my family

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:26.420
to make sure that we
all had the same amount.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:30.950
Over the years, that natural
instinct for data and analysis

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:34.550
has led me to grow into a
thoughtful and analytical

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:38.300
technology professional, and I'm
really grateful to be in a role

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:40.940
here at Google that
allows me to own in

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:42.500
on and grow those skills.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:49.420
Now, let's look at my
certification story.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:52.880
I have bucketed today's story
into three major milestones

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.410
in my journey.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:58.190
They are moving to New York
City, growing my network,

00:01:58.190 --> 00:02:01.550
and deciding to move
forward to become certified.

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:04.160
I have been a user
of Google Cloud tools

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:06.440
for about three
and half years now,

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:09.320
and I have been working in
the cloud space for about that

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:11.120
long as well.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:13.040
My experience really
started when I first

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:15.080
moved to New York City.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:17.690
I moved there for a
marketing engineering program

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:20.370
in the advertising
technology space,

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:24.200
and after that program ended, I
got a job as a platform analyst

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.060
at a small startup.

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:28.040
And I'm really
grateful for that role.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:29.780
That's actually where
I started to get

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:33.040
my hands on GCP experience.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.380
My first step into
Google Cloud was

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:38.000
with BigQuery and
the client interface,

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:41.060
and about a month and a half
after I joined the team,

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:44.440
our company was actually
acquired by another company

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:46.450
and that is where
I was introduced

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:49.360
to how to work in multi
cloud environments

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:51.790
since the company that
acquired us was actually

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:54.760
working with another cloud
service provider at that time.

00:02:56.850 --> 00:03:00.500
So I learned how to integrate
and how to migrate data

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:04.850
across cloud services, and as I
continued to grow in my career,

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:07.460
I eventually became
a consultant where

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:10.910
I was introduced to the
world of cloud architecture

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:14.090
and how to use various
Google Cloud tools to build

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:17.000
a full solution, then
document that solution

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.950
with technical documentation.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:22.820
All of this was
really valuable to me

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:26.030
and it all started with
my move to New York City.

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:29.000
I not only got hands on
Google Cloud experience,

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.970
but I got broad cloud
experience as well.

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:33.890
The takeaway that
I want to note here

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:35.930
is don't be afraid to change.

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:38.160
Have the confidence to
take the first step.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:40.220
Now, moving on to my network.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:42.560
I highly, highly
recommend that you

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:45.500
seek out and nurture
healthy opportunities

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:47.460
to build your network.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.630
This is what really helped
me expand my confidence

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:53.410
as a technology professional.

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:57.410
I grew my network through
meetups, industry events,

00:03:57.410 --> 00:04:01.790
and organizations such as the
Houston Google Developers Group

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:03.770
which partnered with
Women Techmakers for some

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:06.080
of the events I attended.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:08.330
And meetups in New York
City such as the TechYes!

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:12.080
Diversity in Tech Meetup,
along with the Houston GCP user

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:13.350
group.

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:15.180
Check out your
local tech community

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:17.700
to see what's available to you.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:20.230
If there aren't any
or many options,

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:22.810
I encourage you to create one.

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:24.600
Now, I just shared
with you that I

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:27.840
did have quite a bit
of hands-on experience

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:29.790
on the Google Cloud platform.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:32.820
However, what I have come to
realize over the past year

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:36.450
or so is that I was moreso
thinking of myself as someone

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:39.270
who knew how to use a
tool rather than someone

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:43.390
who was a professional
in the cloud industry.

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:45.990
And when that thinking
really turned around

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:49.260
was joining the Google
Cloud Learning Workshop,

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.010
which is one of
Google's diversity,

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:53.340
equity, and
inclusion initiatives

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:56.670
to bring more perspectives
into the cloud industry.

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:01.560
One of my favorite
parts of the workshop

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:03.570
was meeting with
other professionals

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:08.010
with varying years of experience
and varying levels of expertise

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:09.900
in the cloud space.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:12.000
This really helped to
broaden my horizons

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.580
and deepen my understanding
of the use of GCP

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.850
across the use cases.

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:19.940
I realized that some of the
professionals in the room

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:22.670
had been working on technical
infrastructure concepts

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:24.800
before the concept
of cloud computing

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.830
was even widely known.

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:29.690
And I also realized that there
were professionals in the room,

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:33.200
like myself, who were learning
about technical infrastructure

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:36.320
concepts through cloud computing
rather than the other way

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:37.620
around.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:41.000
And what I noticed in
conversations with my cohort

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:44.360
is that I was actually able to
share knowledge and ideas as

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:48.560
if I had been working in this
industry for five or ten years,

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:50.690
and my confidence
grew dramatically

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:53.210
as I realized that I really
did know what I was talking

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:56.180
about as a result of
my hands-on experience

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:58.350
in this new industry.

00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:00.510
When you get that
boost of confidence,

00:06:00.510 --> 00:06:04.470
you continue to grow it, and
that's exactly what I did.

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:07.740
This is and really was a
great turning point for me

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:11.910
as I continue to grow as
a leader and a technology

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:13.020
professional.

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:15.870
Since being able to speak
clearly and with confidence

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:20.400
is an important trait of
being in a leadership role.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.520
My takeaway for you here
is to identify your goals

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:25.680
and surround yourself
with others who have

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:27.450
achieved something similar--

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:30.060
or who have achieved something
bigger than themselves--

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:32.010
and begin to network with them.

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:35.280
You might be amazed at how that
can transform your mindset as

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:36.460
well.

00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:39.450
So now, with all that
being said and done,

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:42.030
as I continue to grow
in my confidence,

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:45.840
I was also introduced to the
world of certification itself.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:49.050
Previously, I had seen
certification as something

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:52.560
that someone with many more
years of experience than I had

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:56.380
would go for, and maybe I could
go for in a few years as well.

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:58.920
However, after my experience
in the learning workshop,

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:00.840
I began to realize that
certification could

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:02.740
be the right route for me.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:04.960
And I also saw it as
a great achievement

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:10.290
to really solidify
my cloud expertise.

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:13.570
And when it comes to the
action of taking the exam,

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:17.780
this is a wonderful story
that I'm proud of as well.

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:21.100
I took the Associate Cloud
Engineer exam in August

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:23.520
and did not pass.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:25.615
It honestly was
so disappointing,

00:07:25.615 --> 00:07:27.990
because I was looking forward
to passing it as many of us

00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:30.240
do when we take exams.

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:33.640
So I did take some time
to be disappointed,

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:36.060
and then I decided to move on.

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:38.400
I took a look at the
areas in the exam

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:40.680
that I felt the most
uncomfortable with

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:44.550
and then I also explored
exam topics in general

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:47.190
across the Google
Cloud certifications.

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:50.370
And throughout
that review period,

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:52.770
after re-evaluating
my skills, I realized

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:55.830
that the data engineering
certification was potentially

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:59.100
the right route for me,
especially since I was coming

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:03.090
from the world of data and I had
hands-on experience with cloud

00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:07.310
technologies in the data space.

00:08:07.310 --> 00:08:10.870
So I took the data
engineering exam and passed.

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:12.550
I was so excited.

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:14.400
It was actually
three weeks after I

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:16.510
had failed the Associate
Cloud Engineer exam

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:18.340
and I was happy and
proud of myself.

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:25.270
Fast forward to February of this
year when after months of study

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:28.090
and months of additional
practice across the Google

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:31.120
Cloud platform tools,
I was able to pass

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:33.190
both the professional
Cloud Architect's

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:38.270
exam and the Associate Cloud
Engineer exam on the same day.

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:40.990
My takeaway for you
here is to stay focused

00:08:40.990 --> 00:08:43.630
and know how you learn
best and let that lead how

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:45.900
you study for the
certification exams

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:47.950
if certification is
one of your goals.

00:08:50.870 --> 00:08:53.930
Becoming Google Cloud Certified
had an important impact

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:55.490
on my career.

00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:59.090
This impact included
immediate career benefits,

00:08:59.090 --> 00:09:01.970
long term professional
gains, and new opportunities

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:05.440
for mentorship.

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:07.780
In terms of immediate
career benefits

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:12.170
in the role that I was in at
the time, becoming certified

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:15.290
opened doors for me to attend a
really cool industry conference

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:18.750
on behalf of my
employer at that time.

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:21.560
I felt like it was a really cool
reward and a great opportunity

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:24.320
for me, and it also
provided me with more

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:26.030
of a voice in the
product engagement

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:29.180
that I was in at that time

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:31.970
Now, onto long-term
professional gains.

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:36.280
A big one has been the
opportunity to work at Google.

00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:42.020
This has been a dream of mine
and a goal of mine for a while.

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:44.070
At Google, I am a
solution engineer

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:47.190
on a team called the Cloud
Solution Studio, and what we do

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:49.120
is really, really cool.

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:51.840
I, along with my
team, build assets

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:55.590
for our sales teams which
demonstrate Google Cloud

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:58.680
solutions across use cases.

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:00.600
In my role, I have
the opportunity

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:04.500
to build on my Google Cloud
certifications and knowledge

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:07.140
to use storytelling, design
thinking, and project

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:12.380
management skills to bring
our solutions to life.

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:14.960
I have been at Google
for over six months now

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:16.768
and it's been really great.

00:10:16.768 --> 00:10:18.560
I got involved in the
Black Googler Network

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:21.620
where I have a great buddy
who has given me advice

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:24.320
and has also just been a great
friend, including giving me

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:27.290
recommendations for
hairdressers which

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:31.370
has been really useful since
I'm new to the Bay Area.

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:35.380
I have also been pretty active
in Google's outreach efforts,

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:38.630
including our Grow with
Google initiative, giving back

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:42.290
to the Google Cloud
Learning workshop,

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:47.040
and other certification
outreach efforts.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:49.490
And last but not least,
getting certified

00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:52.190
has opened doors to mentorship.

00:10:52.190 --> 00:10:53.960
As part of the
learning workshop,

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:56.630
I met someone who is actually
still one of my mentors

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:58.040
to this day.

00:10:58.040 --> 00:11:00.670
I reached out to her and
we stayed in contact,

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:02.440
and now that I am
here at Google,

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:05.240
I am able to meet with
her on a regular basis

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:08.630
and talk about how I am
growing as a professional.

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:12.958
I really do value her advice and
her input into the growth areas

00:11:12.958 --> 00:11:13.625
that we discuss.

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:18.700
Now, before we
wrap up, I do want

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:22.540
to share some takeaways that I
think would be valuable for you

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:24.490
no matter where you
are on your journey

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:26.890
and where you are in your
certification path, as well.

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:31.820
The first is to look
at the growth goals

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:34.220
that you have set for yourself
and have the confidence

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:35.880
to take the first step.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:38.630
It can always feel
daunting to do this.

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:41.000
In my case, it was
daunting to look

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:43.430
at others who were
certified and think, well,

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:45.500
I can be certified too.

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:48.800
Yet it required me to
take the first step.

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:53.090
For me, that looked like being
part of the learning workshop,

00:11:53.090 --> 00:11:56.510
taking courses and studying
diligently, and even taking

00:11:56.510 --> 00:12:00.830
the first step of registering
to take the exams.

00:12:00.830 --> 00:12:03.527
I encourage you to also
have the confidence

00:12:03.527 --> 00:12:05.485
to take the first step
and believe in yourself.

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:12.590
I would also recommend that you
proactively build your network.

00:12:12.590 --> 00:12:16.490
Seek out opportunities to learn
from, partner with, and help

00:12:16.490 --> 00:12:19.040
those who have achieved things
similar to the goals you

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:21.210
have set for yourself.

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:22.800
Also consider
seeking out guidance

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:26.230
from those who have achieved
things bigger than themselves.

00:12:26.230 --> 00:12:28.530
This will help you
to better understand

00:12:28.530 --> 00:12:31.090
what it takes to get
where you need to be

00:12:31.090 --> 00:12:32.970
and it will help
with accountability

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:35.420
along your journey.

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:39.760
It can be really easy to make
goals and then not follow up.

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:42.880
If you have put certification as
a professional or even personal

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:45.970
goal for yourself,
then go for it.

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:48.370
Proactively build your
network and make sure

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:51.900
that you have a level
of accountability.

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:56.110
And consider giving back by
being a mentor to someone else,

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:57.570
especially after
you're certified.

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:03.620
Last but not least, discover
your unique approach.

00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:06.010
This can take on
numerous meanings.

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:08.350
In the certification
space, I would

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:11.260
say to discover the
way you learn best

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:14.020
and craft your study
plan around that.

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:16.720
As an example from
my end, I realized

00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:20.080
that I learn best by
testing myself, getting

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:23.770
hands-on experience, and being
able to tie that experience

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:25.420
to the concepts.

00:13:25.420 --> 00:13:29.440
So, knowing this, I crafted
my personal study plans

00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:32.050
around those principles.

00:13:32.050 --> 00:13:35.470
I recommend that you take
a look at your experiences

00:13:35.470 --> 00:13:38.890
as a learner and see the ways
that you have learned best,

00:13:38.890 --> 00:13:41.500
then take that and
create a personal study

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:43.120
plan for yourself.

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:45.160
Make sure you're being
true to yourself.

00:13:48.210 --> 00:13:50.880
Thank you so much for your time.

00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:53.180
I really appreciate
the opportunity

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:55.820
to share my story
with you and hopefully

00:13:55.820 --> 00:13:59.990
being able to inspire you
to craft a story of your own

00:13:59.990 --> 00:14:02.360
that you can be proud of.

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:04.460
Be sure to check
out the appendix

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:08.600
of this deck for additional
certification resources.

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:12.700
Have a great day, and
perhaps I will see you soon.

